      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 48-year-old man receiving maintenance hemodialysis underwent coronary artery bypass surgery with good results for intractable angina. No complications were observed that could be attributed to the hemodialysis treatment. There appear to be no cogent reasons to arbitrarily exclude this population of patients from consideration for coronary artery bypass surgery."},
